== Releases

The Releases phase covers the handover from development to the product users. Each version passes a structured security gate, is documented internally for traceability, and is communicated to customers so that they can assess and apply the update safely.

.*What this phase covers*
[%collapsible]
====
[mermaid]
----
flowchart TB
    G[Security gate] --> R[Version released]
    A[Authenticity and integrity] --> R
    N[Release documentation] --> R
----

* *Security gate* — verify before shipping that the secure development tasks for this version are closed, that security issues are resolved or accepted, and that the release is signed off.
* *Authenticity and integrity* — give product users a means to verify that what they received is genuine and unaltered.
* *Release documentation* — record internally what the version contains and archive its artifacts, and tell customers what security issues were addressed, what the compatibility constraints are, and how to update.

The controls listed below are the authoritative scope of this phase. Installed extension modules may add further controls here.
====

=== Why it matters

A release is the handoff point between development and the real world. The security gate is your last opportunity to catch unresolved issues before they reach customers. Integrity protection and clear release notes give stakeholders what they need to trust the release and to act on it.

